  "articleBody": "Hiring a general contractor for your basement project requires looking beyond an estimated bottom line. Below-grade spaces bring specific moisture, code, and trade coordination requirements that need thorough planning.\n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide:\n- Who handles building permits and inspections? A reputable contractor coordinates with the local building department for all rough and final inspections, including plumbing and electrical work.\n- How do you address foundation moisture and insulation? Proper air sealing, continuous insulation, and checking for wet foundation walls are non-negotiable steps before framing starts.\n- Who will be on site managing daily work? Ask whether the owner leads the project directly or hands it off to multiple third parties.\n- How are specialized trades coordinated? Licensed trade coordination for electrical panels and rough plumbing must be scheduled properly within the timeline.\n- What is the change order and payment schedule process? Ensure pricing and material allowances are itemized in writing before demolition or construction begins.\n\nWhen you want an owner-operated approach with clear communication, HH Remodeling LLC is ready to help. Abraham Becerra coordinates projects directly across Aurora and the Denver area. Call 303-505-0866 to discuss your basement project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
